❓Question:
Given an integer array nums, find the majority element. The majority element is the element that appears more than n / 2 times in the array.

For example:
Input:  [3,2,3]
Output: 3

✅Approach:
Use the Boyer-Moore Voting Algorithm. Keep a candidate and a count.
If count becomes 0, choose the current element as the new candidate.
If the current element equals the candidate, increase count.
Otherwise, decrease count.
Since the problem guarantees that a majority element always exists, the final candidate is the answer.

Code:
class Solution {
    public int majorityElement(int[] nums) {
        int candidate = nums[0];
        int count = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
            if (count == 0) {
                candidate = nums[i];
                count++;
            }
            else if (candidate == nums[i]) {
                count++;
            }
            else {
                count--;
            }
        }
        return candidate;
    }
}

Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)
